## Release-level versus observation-level provenance

The `terms_url`, `license`, and `attribution` columns in
`inst/extdata/releases.csv` describe the selected release/resource row. They
are not a blanket license for every row in `budget-vintage-observations.csv`
or `myefo-vintage-observations.csv`. Those panels carry
`observation_source_url` and `observation_source_sha256`; use those fields to
identify the source of each derived observation. In particular, PBO-derived
rows remain subject to the PBO terms above even when the enclosing release row
is a Treasury release.

The PBO Historical Fiscal Data product is the source family for
`pbo-historical-observations.csv.gz` and completed historical series. The
separate Historical budget forecasts and measures products are source workbooks
for selected Budget/MYEFO vintage observations. They are distinct PBO
products, and this package does not treat one product's description or terms
as a substitute for the other's.

## Department of Finance distinction

The built-in data.gov.au workbook resources record the Australian Government
Department of Finance attribution and Creative Commons Attribution 3.0
Australia at <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/au/>. This differs
from the Finance website notice at
<https://www.finance.gov.au/about-us/copyright-notice>, which records Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International for website material subject to its
listed exceptions and attribution `© Commonwealth of Australia, Department of
Finance`. Do not substitute the website terms for the resource-level workbook
terms.

## Reuse rule

Retain the source URL, terms URL, license string, attribution, and exact
release/hash metadata when reusing source-derived material. Storage in a local
cache or archive, parsing, normalization, selection, or chart generation does
not itself expand publisher rights or create permission to remove source
notices. Consult the current publisher notice for a particular resource before
commercial reuse, redistribution, or derivative work.
